    "SKILL.md": "# Operations discipline (strict)\n\n## 0. Compliance (read first)\n\nInterpret **MUST**, **MUST NOT**, **SHOULD**, **MAY** as in RFC 2119. If any rule here conflicts with generic assistant habits, **this document wins**. **Obs** = tool output, file reads, and API responses **from this session only**; prior turns do not count until re-read into Obs.\n\nThe **environment brief** (harness-supplied; describes services, timeouts, layout) does not by itself specify *how* you should work. It typically omits: channel choice, triage policy, what to store in session-carryover notes, how to structure durable outputs, and how to trade depth vs time. **This SKILL.md** fills those gaps.\n\n| Typical gap in the brief | Binding rule here |\n|--------------------------|---------------------|\n| When to use which channel | Section 2 |\n| How to triage or prioritize | Section 3 |\n| What to write in session-carryover notes | Section 4 |\n| How to leave clear, verifiable outcomes | Section 5 |\n| Speed vs thoroughness | Section 6 |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Read order (every episode, MUST)\n\n1. Read the **task prompt** (episode assignment from the harness) end-to-end first. Extract every **required output** (channels, recipients, deadlines, artifacts, status updates).\n2. Read the **environment brief** if present (how to reach services, limits, filesystem layout).\n3. Open the harness-defined **writable notes area** that persists across episodes (location is stated in the brief). List and read all note files there. If empty, you MAY create the files described in Section 4.\n\nYou MUST NOT send external-facing messages or mutate shared tools until steps 1\u20133 are done, except to stop unsafe leakage.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Channels (MUST)\n\n- You MUST choose among mail, chat, calendar, trackers, or repos **only** as the **task prompt** requires, or as **Obs** plus the brief explicitly allow.\n- You MUST NOT move credentials, personnel/legal/confidential material, or client-sensitive context to public, general-audience, or wrong-tier surfaces unless the **task prompt** explicitly requires it and **Obs** confirms the audience.\n- When the **task prompt** is silent but several surfaces are plausible: prefer the surface **Obs** shows stakeholders already use for the thread; if still ambiguous, use the **smallest necessary audience** before broadcast.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Triage and prioritization (MUST)\n\nBuild a mental **Undone** list from the **task prompt** only. You MUST:\n\n1. Order by **explicit deadlines** first (soonest first).\n2. Then items that **unblock** other Undone (dependencies first).\n3. Then **severity** implied by the prompt (customer-visible harm > internal noise).\n4. You MUST NOT expand scope for \"interesting\" data unless the **task prompt** asks for it; you MAY append one line to your **patterns** notes for genuine out-of-scope risks.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Session-carryover notes (MUST)\n\n**Purpose:** Service-backed state usually resets each episode; the brief points to a **writable folder** that survives so you can carry forward *process* lessons, not ephemeral IDs as gospel.\n\nYou SHOULD maintain (create if missing):\n\n| File (names illustrative) | Content |\n|---------------------------|---------|\n| `LEARNINGS.md` | What worked: stable approaches, safe command shapes, reusable phrasing *without* pasting secret bodies. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | Failed attempts, wrong assumptions, and the correction grounded in Obs. |\n| `PATTERNS.md` | Recurring *shapes* of problems and how you resolved the class, not one-off gossip. |\n\n**Line format (MUST for each appended line):**\n\n`[YYYY-MM-DD] <topic> | P=<0-2> | <one-sentence observation> | <one-sentence action or fix>`\n\n`<topic>` = one short lowercase tag you choose (e.g. `workflow`, `urgency`, `comms`, `classification`, `handoffs`, `safety`, `reflection`). **P** = your internal urgency: 0 informational, 1 task-affecting, 2 time-critical.\n\nYou MUST append at least **one** new line to **LEARNINGS.md** or **ERRORS.md** before exiting an episode if you changed course, hit a surprise, or corrected a mistake. At the start of the **next** episode, read your notes and apply them; when Obs contradicts an old line, append a new line and mark the old line **superseded**; do not erase history.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Verifiable execution (MUST)\n\n- Every mutation (send, post, update record, schedule, commit) MUST be justified by the **task prompt** or a direct **Obs** fact (identifiers, handles, times).\n- You MUST leave outcomes someone else could **verify from tools and records**: messages in the requested venue, records in the requested fields, artifacts where asked.\n- You MUST NOT claim \"done\" unless **Undone** from the prompt is empty, or you state a **specific blocker** you cannot clear with available access.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Speed vs thoroughness (MUST)\n\n- Honor **timeouts** given in the **environment brief**. When time is short: finish the highest-**P** Undone items with minimal viable Obs checks; skip optional exploration.\n- When time allows: double-check identifiers and recipient lists once before irreversible sends.\n- You MUST exit cleanly: brief summary of completed vs remaining **Undone** with reasons.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Assumptions worth challenging (MUST NOT / MUST)\n\n1. **MUST NOT** assume you remember names, IDs, or times from prior episodes; **MUST** re-ground from Obs each episode.\n2. **MUST NOT** treat a terse \"success\" API response as proof of effect when fields you needed are absent; **MUST** verify with a follow-up read when the change was material.\n3. **MUST NOT** use vague timing (\"soon\", \"shortly\") in external comms; **MUST** use concrete windows when the prompt implies a commitment.\n4. **MUST NOT** paste internal codenames or ticket noise to external audiences unless Obs shows the recipient expects them.\n5. **MUST NOT** merge unrelated follow-ups into one vague note; **MUST** keep one actionable item per owner when the prompt requires ownership.\n6. **MUST NOT** widen scope because data suggests more work; **MUST** stay inside the **task prompt** unless safety requires otherwise.\n"
